{"availability":"available","full":"chuckhalliday/JSON-Hit-Builder","name":"JSON-Hit-Builder","description":"Compose songs in the browser","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2022-09-04T07:28:35Z","updated":"2026-10-11T06:52:03Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://node-composer.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://node-composer.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T03:02:07.440Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T03:02:07.440Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T03:02:07.440Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:44:20.995Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-11T23:57:18.782Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-18T03:02:07.440Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Welcome to the JSON Hit Builder, a web application dedicated to music composition and exploration. You can experience it live at node-composer.vercel.app. This project was initially inspired by my tinkering with Sonic Pi, a live coding music program written in Ruby for those unfamiliar.","I set out designing this application with the idea of facilitating musical composition by generating arrays for concurrent instruments, triggered by MIDI hits from enum strings based on time-value arrays. The idea was to have an application that constructs these arrays to synchronize based on rhythmic logic and/or genre. Opting for JavaScript, my language of choice, I took the personal opportunity to delve into TypeScript, appreciating its bug avoidance and code navigation benefits."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/chuckhalliday/JSON-Hit-Builder/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3e31d628597c81fccb4a6a5be69ff1a8a605a3cccaba7112fd44e43fba2bcdfa","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T23:44:21.230Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:44:21.230Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Welcome to the JSON Hit Builder, a web application dedicated to music composition and exploration. You